            "content": "---\nname: agent-worktree-bases-on-master\ndescription: Agent tool isolation:\"worktree\" bases the new worktree on master, not the current branch HEAD, so subagents silently work against a stale tree\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\n`Agent` with `isolation: \"worktree\"` creates the worktree from **master**, not from\nthe branch you have checked out. A subagent dispatched from a feature branch lands on\n`master` and never mentions it.\n\n**Why:** on `quality/mutation-testing` (Sept 2026) three subagents were dispatched from\nbranch HEAD `99dd605b` and all three came up at `30fc48ba` (master), missing the 11,496\nlines of tests the branch had already added. They were about to write duplicate suites and\nclobber upstream files on merge. A fourth agent launched through `cursor-agent\n--worktree-base quality/mutation-testing` was correct, because that flag was passed\nexplicitly. One subagent caught it and asked; the other two never noticed.\n\nThe damage is silent and two-sided: line numbers in any artifact keyed to the real HEAD\n(a mutation report, a review diff, a coverage map) do not match the tree the agent reads,\nand edits to files that changed on the branch overwrite that work at harvest time.\n\n**How to apply:**\n\n- Put the base check in the agent prompt itself, as the first instruction:\n  `git log --oneline -1` and, if it is not the expected SHA,\n  `git merge --ff-only <sha>`. A clean worktree makes that a pure fast-forward that\n  destroys nothing.\n- Verify from the parent too — `git worktree list` shows every agent worktree with its\n  HEAD, so one call confirms all of them at once.\n- Fix it *before* the agent writes anything. Fast-forwarding a clean worktree is free;\n  after edits exist, `merge --ff-only` refuses and you are reconciling by hand.\n- `git reset --hard` and `git checkout -- <path>` are blocked by Safety Net here.\n  `git switch -C <branch> <ref>` moves a branch pointer, and\n  `git show <ref>:<path> > <path>` restores one file, both without tripping it.\n\nSee [[mutation-harvest-runs-three-gates]] for the harvest-side gates and\n[[subagents-can-destroy-uncommitted-work]] for the shared-worktree hazard this avoids.\n",
